4) Sentinel Module Suite (Product Boxes)

Sentinel modules are independent products that interlock through
LAIRS (mind) and SentiNet (fabric).

Sentinel Agent

Purpose: Integrity, telemetry, and runtime enforcement

File, process, and configuration integrity monitoring

Runtime anomaly and drift detection (Watchdog functionality is here)

Evidence generation for governance decisions

Secure export into LAIRS and Metatron’s Gate

Host-level enforcement and observation

Metatron’s Gate (Quorum & Governance)

Purpose: Intent governance and authority control

Explicit intent declaration for sensitive actions

Multi-party quorum enforcement (Machine / AI / Human)

Observe-only and enforcement modes

Cryptographic approval and denial tracking

Append-only, causally chained audit log

Prevents unilateral system modification by design

Sentinel Gate

Purpose: Policy enforcement and controlled access

Entry control into SentiNet fabric

Policy validation and trust scoring

Controlled ingress / egress

Fail-closed by design

Sentinel AV

Purpose: Malware detection and quarantine

Local scanning (no cloud dependency)

Quarantine workflows

Trust degradation signals into LAIRS

Integrates with Agent and Gate

Sentinel Forge

Purpose: Governed system evolution

Patch and configuration proposals

Staging and validation workflows

Rollback-first design

Human approval required for apply

LNT (Leave No Trace)

Purpose: Data minimization and audit hygiene

Evidence minimization

Log retention controls

Privacy-preserving audit support

No Sentinel module can:

bypass LAIRS policy gates

bypass Metatron’s Gate quorum

bypass SentiNet zone controls

self-authorize irreversible actions

5) Governance Flow (Human Root Authority)

This is the platform’s non-negotiable safety model.

(Observe) → (Analyze) → (Propose) → (Approve) → (Apply) → (Verify)

